---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy · Centre Pullz"
  description="What Centre Pullz does and does not collect: no accounts, no tracking cookies of our own, and a plain list of the third parties your browser contacts when you load a page."
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {site.legalUpdated}</p>
    <p class="lede">
      Centre Pullz is a static reference site. There are no accounts, no logins,
      no comment boxes and no forms that send anything to us. This page describes
      exactly what happens when you visit.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect directly</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. We do not run our own analytics, we do not set our own cookies, and
      we have no server-side database that stores anything about you. We could not
      identify a visitor if we wanted to.
    </p>
    <p>
      The search box on the database page runs entirely inside your browser. What
      you type is never transmitted to us — it only filters a list that was already
      downloaded with the page. Your search terms may appear in the page URL so
      that results can be bookmarked or shared; that URL stays in your browser
      unless you choose to share it.
    </p>

    <h2>What our host processes</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes
      technical request data — including your IP address — to deliver pages and
      protect against abuse. This is handled under Cloudflare's own privacy terms,
      and we do not receive per-visitor reports from it.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties your browser contacts</h2>
    <p>
      Some page content is loaded directly from other companies' servers. When
      that happens, those servers necessarily see your IP address, your browser
      user-agent, and the page you came from. We have no control over, and no
      access to, what they do with it:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Fonts</strong> (<span class="mono">fonts.googleapis.com</span>,
        <span class="mono">fonts.gstatic.com</span>) — serves the typefaces used across
        the site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Prize manufacturers</strong> (including
        <span class="mono">bsp-prize.jp</span>, <span class="mono">furyuprize.com</span>,
        <span class="mono">segaplaza.jp</span>, <span class="mono">taito.co.jp</span>) —
        product photographs are shown directly from the manufacturers' own sites
        rather than copied onto ours.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>X / Twitter</strong> (<span class="mono">pbs.twimg.com</span>) — the
        annotated measurement photographs are shown from their original posts.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you would rather not contact these servers, a content blocker or
      script/image blocker will stop them; the measurement data itself is plain
      text in the page and will still be readable.
    </p>

    {site.hasAds ? (
      <>
        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          This site shows advertising supplied by Google. Google and its partners
          may use cookies or similar identifiers to serve and measure ads,
          including ads based on your prior visits to this or other websites.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can opt out of personalised advertising from Google at
          <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Google Ads Settings</a>, and opt out of personalisation from many other
          vendors at
          <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            aboutads.info/choices</a>. Where required by law, you will be asked for
          consent before any non-essential cookie is set, and you can change that
          choice at any time.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          This site currently carries no advertising and no advertising cookies.
          If that changes, this policy will be updated before any ad code is added,
          and — where the law requires it — you will be asked for consent before
          any non-essential cookie is set.
        </p>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a general-audience reference and is not directed at children
      under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone,
      including children.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy laws including the GDPR (EU/UK), the CCPA/CPRA (California) and
      Japan's APPI give you rights to access, correct, delete or restrict the use
      of personal data held about you. Because we hold no personal data about
      visitors, there is nothing for us to return or erase. Requests about data
      held by the third parties listed above need to go to those companies
      directly.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the "last updated" date above changes with it.
      Material changes — in particular, introducing advertising or analytics —
      will be reflected here before the change goes live.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    {site.contactEmail ? (
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="mono note">A contact address for this site has not been published yet.</p>
    )}
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .note {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
